# Line-ending contract for files whose BYTES are the assertion.
#
# Windows CI runners (actions/checkout) and most Windows dev boxes behave like
# core.autocrlf=true, which hands out CRLF copies of LF blobs at checkout time.
# That silently breaks exact comparisons, so anything compared byte-for-byte or
# line-anchored is pinned to LF here instead of being left to whatever each
# machine happens to have configured.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto` and no blanket rules, so adding this
# file cannot renormalize unrelated content. PowerShell follows core.autocrlf.
# Batch files are committed with literal CRLF bytes: git archive uses blobs,
# so eol=crlf alone would still ship LF in the downloadable ZIP.
*.cmd -text whitespace=cr-at-eol

# §17.2 golden Status panels - tests/status-display.test.ps1 diffs them line by
# line and asserts they contain no CR.
codex-quota-keeper/tests/golden/*.txt text eol=lf

# The packager's gate reads this file with an anchored ^...$ regex
# (tests/build-release.test.ps1), so a CR at line end breaks the match.
codex-quota-keeper/.gitignore text eol=lf
